digraph account_payable_process_46 {
	graph [rankdir=LR]
	START_NODE [label="" shape=circle width=0.3]
	subgraph CLUSTER_0 {
		"send to the vendor accounting department" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" [shape=box]
		"send to the vendor accounting department" -> "create a receiving report"
		"double check a three-way match" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" -> "double check a three-way match"
		"AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_GXKS" [label="+" fixedsize=true shape=diamond width=0.5]
		"double check a three-way match" -> "AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_GXKS"
		"store in paid invoice file" [shape=box]
		"AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_GXKS" -> "store in paid invoice file"
		"schedule the payment" [shape=box]
		"AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_GXKS" -> "schedule the payment"
		"AND_JOIN--4. Payment_GXKS" [label="+" fixedsize=true shape=diamond width=0.5]
		"store in paid invoice file" -> "AND_JOIN--4. Payment_GXKS"
		"schedule the payment" -> "AND_JOIN--4. Payment_GXKS"
	}
	START_NODE -> "send to the vendor accounting department"
	END_NODE [label="" shape=doublecircle width=0.2]
	"AND_JOIN--4. Payment_GXKS" -> END_NODE
	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The text below is about the account payable process. It begins when you send to the vendor accounting department. 
When sending to the vendor accounting department is completed, creating a receiving report needs to be done. 
When creating a receiving report is completed, you need to double check a three-way match.
When doubling check a three-way match is completed, the next tasks should be storing in paid invoice file and scheduling the payment, they should be done in parallel. 
The process is now completed. 
"
}
